  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "game-description-1ea2a3ec-faf6-4c5c-bdd2-8db02c6e6979-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Dance organizes bodily movement into expressive, rhythmic, social, or ceremonial forms. It may follow established steps and choreography or develop through improvisation, and it can be performed alone, with a partner, or in groups. Music is a frequent companion, but movement can also establish its own timing."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-1ea2a3ec-faf6-4c5c-bdd2-8db02c6e6979-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Dance is included here as a broad field of embodied play rather than one game with a universal rulebook. Social dances, performance traditions, and competitive dancesport place different values on participation, interpretation, technique, and judging. Their histories belong to many communities, so a single inventor or release date would be misleading."
    },
